Keep the cursor after its text when a resize reflows a line (backport)

Backport of upstream c44afa625 ("fix: preserve active cursor position
during reflow", Riccardo Mazzarini, on main for 1.3.2; not on
1.3.x). In v1.3.1 a resize clamps every tracked pin that sits in a line's
trailing blanks to the destination row where the source row began. The
live cursor usually sits on such a blank, right after what was printed.
When the text still wraps at the new width, the clamp drops the cursor
inside the text, and every later resize carries it there faithfully.
Widening a window by dragging passes through such widths, so a prompt
printed in a narrow window ends with the cursor in the middle of it.

The fix passes the cursor's own pin into the reflow, exempts it from the
clamp and counts the blanks before it as part of the line, so they wrap
with the text. Other tracked pins keep the clamp. The first two tests are
upstream's; the third reproduces the drag: 40 -> 50 -> 80 columns.

